    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b73355af-8562-58ac-92ab-a09e083ca7d0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{dy}{dt}= \\\\ \\frac{y^{3} - y^{2} - 6 y}{y - 3}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nFirst keep the original domain: $y - 3\\ne0$.\n\nTest whether $f(c)=0$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}f(c)= \\\\ \\frac{c^{3} - c^{2} - 6 c}{c - 3}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n- For $c=-3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=3$, $c - 3=0$ violates the original domain, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=0$ and $y=-2$.",
